From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] zygote: CAP_NET_ADMIN for Bluetooth without paranoid network

Bluetooth PAN (the Car Thing as a client of the iPhone's Personal Hotspot)
failed: the Bluetooth stack could not create the bt-pan TAP interface, so
IpClient found no interface ("Failed to find InterfaceParams for bt-pan").
TUNSETIFF for a new device needs CAP_NET_ADMIN. Android 9 gives it to the
Bluetooth process only through CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK (the net_admin
group), and the Car Thing kernel has that option off. Grant CAP_NET_ADMIN to
the Bluetooth process directly. SELinux already allows net_admin for the
bluetooth domain.

---
--- a/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
+++ b/core/jni/com_android_internal_os_Zygote.cpp
@@ -826,6 +826,10 @@
       capabilities |= (1LL << CAP_NET_RAW);
       capabilities |= (1LL << CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE);
       capabilities |= (1LL << CAP_SYS_NICE);
+      // PlayThing: the kernel has no CONFIG_ANDROID_PARANOID_NETWORK, which gives
+      // CAP_NET_ADMIN to the net_admin group (Bluetooth is in it). The Bluetooth stack needs it
+      // to create and bring up the bt-pan TAP interface for PAN (TUNSETIFF, SIOCSIFFLAGS).
+      capabilities |= (1LL << CAP_NET_ADMIN);
     }
 
     // Grant CAP_BLOCK_SUSPEND to processes that belong to GID "wakelock"
